    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35244" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-mŏlo</span></b> , ĕre,
			v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>to grind up.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">piperis grana,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ser. Samm. 19, 334</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, in mal. part.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alienas uxores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 1, 2, 35</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Petr. 23</span></i>.</div>
